# DESCRIPTION

Section 6 holds the formats of files and messages: what a program reads or writes, byte by byte or line by line.

Records are written in one format, directives: one a line, a name and then its words, split at spaces and tabs, with `#` starting a comment, as in manifest(6), driver(6) and the header of guide(6).
A program that reads directives stops at anything it doesn't know, with the file and the line, rather than skipping it.
Tables are TSV, a tab between fields.

A format whose reader has a table of directives has a page that defines every one of them.

